#: ../../Glossary.rst:2
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:4
msgid ""
"Below you will find some common \"uncommon\" words that are used in the "
"CharaChorder community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:9
msgid "3D Press"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:11
msgid ""
"When a switch is activated by pushing it normal to the surface of the "
"device (same as an ordinary keyboard switch)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:13
msgid "Active Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:15
msgid ""
"Nudges your mouse one pixel every minute or so to keep your computer from"
" sleeping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:17
msgid "Ambidextrous Throwover (aka Mirror Mode)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:19
msgid ""
"Entry mode designed for one-handed typing. Characters from the opposite "
"hand are mirrored to the hand which activates this feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:21
msgid "Arpeggiate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:23
msgid ""
"A quick, single key press and release to indicate a suffix, prefix, or "
"modifier to be associated with a chord."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:25
msgid "Chentry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:27
msgid ""
"Shorthand for 'character entry', or typing on a chording-enabled device "
"letter by letter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:29
msgid "Chord Modifiers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:31
msgid ""
"Inputs which, when included with a chord, change the prefix, suffix, "
"capitalization, conjugation, part of speech, language, or structure of a "
"chord.  Note, these can be used arpeggiately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:33
msgid "Compound Chords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:35
msgid ""
"Multiple chords which behave differently when used together in context "
"(not yet user programmable). Example: know + ledge = knowledge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:37
msgid "Cursor Warping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:39
msgid ""
"When your cursor or mouse position moves (\"warps\") based on a chord. "
"Example: Chord \" with DUP to create \"\" and warp your cursor inside "
"\"\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:41
msgid "DUP (duplicate) key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:43
msgid ""
"In character entry, it repeats your last input. In chorded entry, it is "
"used for words with repeating letters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:49
msgid "Fluid Chorded/Character Entry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:51
msgid ""
"Default text entry mode for CharaChorder. Output characters individually "
"(like a keyboard) OR press and release multiple characters of a chord "
"simultaneously to output a chord."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:45
msgid "Forced Chord Phenomenon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:47
msgid ""
"The experience of typing a word in character entry feeling unnatural due "
"to the development of muscle memory for chording that word."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:54
msgid "GTM (Generative Text Menu)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:56
msgid ""
"A text-based menu accessible anywhere you type. It allows access to "
"various device settings and features without software. See "
":doc:`GenerativeTextMenu`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:58
msgid "Impulse Chord"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:60
msgid ""
"An 'on-the-fly' custom chord that can be spontaneously created anywhere "
"you can type via the GTM. See :ref:`Chords:Impulse chording`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:62
msgid "Macro"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:64
msgid "Sequence of mouse and/or keyboard actions assigned to a chord."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:65
msgid "Spurring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Glossary.rst:67
msgid ""
"A 'chording only' mode which outputs chords on a press rather than a "
"press & release. Enables jumping from one chord to another without "
"releasing everything. It can provide significant speed gains with "
"chording, but also takes away the flexibility of character entry. "
"Spurring also helps new users learn how to chord by eliminating the need "
"to focus on timing."
msgstr ""

